For the first day of being president, I would be very excited to get stuff done. As I walk through the white house my eyes would be wide open because you always hear about the white house and how it's important and actually being in it is fascinating. I would imagine that I am taking the same steps that many presidents before me have taken. After all my stuff and family are settled. I will begin my job by entering the office and taking a seat at the Oval Office desk. 
 	As I am at my desk, first I will create laws that would better serve the people of the country. For example, let's assume I would be entering office this current January. Right now there is a huge influx of immigrants in the country. I will close the border and reassess the situation. Immigrants who are here illegally can stay but need to have a job and show that they are contributing to the country's growth because it would be more work to have to remove and place the immigrants out of the country. Then for the border in order for people to enter they will need to cross legally and show proof of documentation. Yes, I understand that most of the immigrants are coming here for better opportunities than their countries are offering. but just like in an emergency in an airplane. They recommend that you put your mask on before you help others. We as a country need to tackle our problems before helping others. On the first day, the main goal is to tackle as many problems as I can but I can not be too hasty to fix these problems that they are not thought through properly.

	On my last day of being president, I would spend it reminiscing about what I accomplished throughout the four years. During my alone time during the day, I will try to wander the walls of the white house and look back at all the presidents who came before. Asking myself “I did enough to help the country and its people”. At last, I will thank the wonderful staff that trusted and followed the direction I took to get the country to where it is on my last day. As well as greet the new first family ensuring that they move the country in a direction that assures freedom and justice for all.
